# GlyphGuardian — Multilingual design principles

Unicode enables a multilingual internet. Non-Latin letters and mixed writing systems are not inherently suspicious.

The current website includes examples and a browser-local character inspector. Research should involve multilingual contributors, representative legitimate text, and explicit false-positive evaluation before any protection claims or warnings are introduced.

Browser extensions and integrations remain development goals. The 2025 global expansion vision is preserved in docs/history/GLOBAL-2025.md; it is a historical proposal, not a record of deployed protections or institutional partnerships.

See ROADMAP and TECHNOTES.md for current scope.
